1
00:00:00,840 --> 00:00:08,140
In the year 845, the Colossal Titan
and the Armored Titan suddenly appeared

2
00:00:08,340 --> 00:00:12,560
and destroyed one of humanity's walls...
and everyday life with it.

3
00:00:12,770 --> 00:00:17,350
And then, finally freed
from their century-long hunger,

4
00:00:17,560 --> 00:00:19,690
the Titans overran humankind once again.

5
00:00:19,900 --> 00:00:23,730
Stop!

6
00:00:23,940 --> 00:00:27,070
Humanity abandoned Wall Maria,

7
00:00:27,280 --> 00:00:30,780
lost 20% of its population
and one-third of its territory,

8
00:00:30,990 --> 00:00:35,200
and was forced to retreat behind Wall Rose.

9
00:00:53,260 --> 00:00:58,100
Unknown are the names
of the flowers that have been trampled

10
00:00:58,310 --> 00:01:03,570
Birds have fallen to the earth
and long for the wind

11
00:01:03,770 --> 00:01:08,650
Prayers won't solve anything

12
00:01:08,860 --> 00:01:13,990
Only the will to fight
can change the here and now!

13
00:01:14,200 --> 00:01:19,290
O pigs who laugh at the resolve
to walk over corpses to move forward

14
00:01:19,500 --> 00:01:21,830
Livestock complacency? False prosperity?

15
00:01:22,040 --> 00:01:24,710
Give us the freedom of dying,
starving wolves!

16
00:01:24,920 --> 00:01:30,090
The humiliation of being caged
is what triggers us to fight back

17
00:01:30,300 --> 00:01:35,390
We hunters slaughter prey
beyond the castle walls,

18
00:01:35,600 --> 00:01:40,600
consumed with surging bloodlust,

19
00:01:40,810 --> 00:01:47,740
as our crimson bows and arrows
pierce scarlet holes into the twilight

20
00:02:09,984 --> 00:02:14,989
The Night of the Closing Ceremony: Humanity's Comeback, Part 2

21
00:02:21,440 --> 00:02:24,520
Pick up the pace! Run, you lead-footed laggards!

22
00:02:26,070 --> 00:02:27,980
What's your problem, Arlelt?!

23
00:02:28,190 --> 00:02:29,740
You're dragging your feet!

24
00:02:30,820 --> 00:02:34,820
Too heavy for you?!
Maybe you'd prefer I let you drop your gear?!

25
00:02:36,120 --> 00:02:40,080
If this were a real mission,
you'd be Titan food by now!

26
00:02:41,870 --> 00:02:43,580
Damn...

27
00:02:43,790 --> 00:02:45,250
Give it here!

28
00:02:46,130 --> 00:02:50,920
You're gonna fail out at this rate!
We're being graded today!

29
00:02:51,130 --> 00:02:54,010
But you'll get points marked off too if you do that...

30
00:02:54,220 --> 00:02:58,510
Then make the grade without
getting found out! Before I change my mind!

31
00:03:01,310 --> 00:03:03,390
Reiner Braun...

32
00:03:04,810 --> 00:03:07,860
Stalwart in both mind and body,

33
00:03:08,070 --> 00:03:10,860
and well-respected by his comrades.

34
00:03:12,950 --> 00:03:16,320
I refuse to be a burden! Even if it costs me my life!

35
00:03:20,950 --> 00:03:22,750
Armin Arlelt.

36
00:03:22,960 --> 00:03:24,370
Although lacking in physical strength,

37
00:03:24,580 --> 00:03:27,420
his aptitude in the classroom is extraordinary.

38
00:03:44,690 --> 00:03:46,350
Annie Leonhart.

39
00:03:46,560 --> 00:03:48,440
Her slice attacks are absolutely flawless,

40
00:03:48,650 --> 00:03:51,530
but her reclusive tendencies make her
a poor fit for coordinated efforts.

41
00:03:51,730 --> 00:03:53,190
Bertholdt Hoover.

42
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:57,660
He possesses remarkable potential,
but lacks aggressiveness.

43
00:03:57,870 --> 00:03:59,370
Jean Kirschtein.

44
00:03:59,580 --> 00:04:01,410
Top-class omni-directional mobility.

45
00:04:01,620 --> 00:04:05,410
But his volatile personality
tends to cause friction with others.

46
00:04:07,540 --> 00:04:09,790
I can't slice as good as those two!

47
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:12,500
I'll just have to find the Titans before them!

48
00:04:15,010 --> 00:04:17,010
If anyone gets into the Military Police...

49
00:04:17,220 --> 00:04:18,640
...it'll be me!

50
00:04:21,680 --> 00:04:23,470
Thanks for the help, Jean!

51
00:04:24,600 --> 00:04:27,060
Following you was a good idea!

52
00:04:30,060 --> 00:04:32,400
Hooray!

53
00:04:33,570 --> 00:04:35,030
Sasha Braus.

54
00:04:35,240 --> 00:04:37,200
She has unconventionally good intuition,

55
00:04:37,400 --> 00:04:40,490
but also demonstrates poor teamwork as a result.

56
00:04:40,700 --> 00:04:42,370
Conny Springer.

57
00:04:42,580 --> 00:04:47,540
He excels at executing quick turns,
but is also a bit dim-witted.

58
00:04:47,750 --> 00:04:49,330
Here they come.

59
00:04:57,260 --> 00:04:59,970
Damn! Shallower than Mikasa again!

60
00:05:00,180 --> 00:05:01,970
Mikasa Ackermann.

61
00:05:02,180 --> 00:05:04,430
Completely proficient in every area.

62
00:05:04,640 --> 00:05:08,520
It's apt to say she's an unmatched,
unprecedented genius.

63
00:05:08,730 --> 00:05:10,150
Eren Jaeger.

64
00:05:10,350 --> 00:05:12,440
He has no real specialties,
but he's improved his grades

65
00:05:12,650 --> 00:05:14,980
with his unparalleled effort.

66
00:05:15,190 --> 00:05:19,820
And he possesses twice
the sense of purpose than anyone else.

67
00:05:35,630 --> 00:05:37,880
Oww!

68
00:05:38,090 --> 00:05:41,390
Sorry. I'm not good at holding back.

69
00:05:42,720 --> 00:05:45,930
Now it's your turn to be the rogue.

70
00:05:46,930 --> 00:05:48,560
What's the matter?

71
00:05:48,770 --> 00:05:51,810
I don't get this training.

72
00:05:52,020 --> 00:05:54,820
Why would soldiers fight other people?

73
00:05:55,020 --> 00:05:58,900
Only an idiot would take on a target barehanded.

74
00:06:01,110 --> 00:06:03,950
That's irresponsible thinking.

75
00:06:04,160 --> 00:06:05,910
We're soldiers.

76
00:06:06,120 --> 00:06:10,250
There are times we can't run away,
no matter how bad the situation is.

77
00:06:10,460 --> 00:06:12,920
No matter what the enemy is,
we have to be ready for it,

78
00:06:13,130 --> 00:06:16,550
whether it means
using cannons or combat techniques.

79
00:06:16,750 --> 00:06:21,260
I believe that's the responsibility of a strong soldier.

80
00:06:22,510 --> 00:06:24,720
Anyway, look there.

81
00:06:26,220 --> 00:06:28,930
Oh, that's Annie.

82
00:06:29,140 --> 00:06:32,190
She's slacking off without
the commandant noticing again.

83
00:06:32,390 --> 00:06:36,070
All right, Eren. That slouch needs a talking-to.

84
00:06:36,270 --> 00:06:40,490
Let's teach her how a soldier's supposed to act.

85
00:06:40,690 --> 00:06:42,150
Huh?

86
00:06:45,530 --> 00:06:47,740
Not fond of the commandant's head-butts?

87
00:06:47,950 --> 00:06:50,370
If you don't wanna end up any shorter,

88
00:06:50,580 --> 00:06:53,500
think back to when you first came here
and start taking things seriously.

89
00:06:53,710 --> 00:06:56,040
Hey, why are you being so rude?

90
00:06:59,050 --> 00:07:00,760
Man, she's mad.

91
00:07:00,960 --> 00:07:03,430
I thought she looked scary enough as it is,

92
00:07:03,630 --> 00:07:06,050
but that's nothing compared to when she's pissed.

93
00:07:06,260 --> 00:07:07,970
All right! Get started, Eren!

94
00:07:08,180 --> 00:07:09,600
Me?!

95
00:07:15,730 --> 00:07:18,070
You know the drill, right, Annie?

96
00:07:18,270 --> 00:07:19,530
Here I come!

97
00:07:23,860 --> 00:07:25,700
Wh-What the...?!

98
00:07:25,910 --> 00:07:27,870
She kicked my leg?!

99
00:07:28,740 --> 00:07:30,200
Can I go now?

100
00:07:30,410 --> 00:07:34,040
No! The drill's not over until you take the dagger!

101
00:07:35,290 --> 00:07:36,380
Wait, Annie!

102
00:07:36,580 --> 00:07:38,880
You're supposed to do this a certain way!

103
00:07:46,590 --> 00:07:48,680
There.

104
00:07:48,890 --> 00:07:51,930
Now it's your turn to attack me.

105
00:07:52,140 --> 00:07:53,810
N-No... I'm not...

106
00:07:54,020 --> 00:07:56,060
Do it, Reiner.

107
00:07:56,270 --> 00:08:00,320
I thought you wanted to teach her
about a soldier's responsibility?

108
00:08:03,490 --> 00:08:08,280
Yeah. Sometimes a soldier can't back down.

109
00:08:08,490 --> 00:08:10,530
This is one of those times!

110
00:08:15,290 --> 00:08:17,120
That's an amazing technique.

111
00:08:17,330 --> 00:08:19,590
Who did you learn it from?

112
00:08:19,790 --> 00:08:20,880
My father.

113
00:08:21,090 --> 00:08:24,720
- Your dad came up with that move?
- What does it matter?

114
00:08:24,920 --> 00:08:27,970
There's no point to any of this.

115
00:08:28,180 --> 00:08:30,470
You mean this training?

116
00:08:30,680 --> 00:08:33,930
We aren't graded on our hand-to-hand combat skills.

117
00:08:34,140 --> 00:08:36,980
Most people brush it off, like them.

118
00:08:37,190 --> 00:08:40,860
Because only the top ten cadets
are allowed to join the Military Police

119
00:08:41,060 --> 00:08:43,820
and serve in the interior.

120
00:08:44,030 --> 00:08:48,450
The only ones who take it seriously
are naive idiots like you...

121
00:08:48,660 --> 00:08:50,910
...or just ordinary idiots.

122
00:08:51,120 --> 00:08:52,950
Crap! The commandant!

123
00:08:55,410 --> 00:08:59,790
For some reason, in this world,
the better you are at fighting Titans

124
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:02,380
the further you can get from them.

125
00:09:02,590 --> 00:09:04,960
How do you think this farce came about?

126
00:09:05,170 --> 00:09:08,010
I don't know... That's a good question!

127
00:09:12,300 --> 00:09:16,520
Maybe because it's human nature?

128
00:09:22,770 --> 00:09:25,690
Anyway, I refuse to be stupid enough

129
00:09:25,900 --> 00:09:30,450
to play "Soldier" in this inane world.

130
00:09:33,370 --> 00:09:36,700
Looks like you're not much of a warrior at all.

131
00:09:38,500 --> 00:09:41,710
I was so caught up in getting stronger
that I never realized it.

132
00:09:41,920 --> 00:09:44,540
It's such a clear contradiction...

133
00:09:44,750 --> 00:09:47,590
They're honing their Titan-killing skills

134
00:09:47,800 --> 00:09:50,760
just to get away from the Titans!

135
00:09:55,310 --> 00:09:57,020
It can't be helped.

136
00:09:57,220 --> 00:10:01,100
Before Wall Maria fell, only the Scouts
needed omni-directional mobility,

137
00:10:01,310 --> 00:10:03,690
and they're a small regiment.

138
00:10:03,900 --> 00:10:06,480
- That put ODM expertise at risk...
- Give it a strong blast for just a second.

139
00:10:06,690 --> 00:10:11,150
- ...so this was a way to prevent its decline.
- Relying on inertia will save you gas.

140
00:10:11,360 --> 00:10:12,990
Easier said than done.

141
00:10:13,200 --> 00:10:16,950
Yeah, maybe not everyone can pull it off...

142
00:10:18,410 --> 00:10:20,250
...but there's no harm in knowing about it,

143
00:10:20,460 --> 00:10:22,580
if you wanna join the Military Police.

144
00:10:22,790 --> 00:10:25,420
Yeah! I'd love to get in!

145
00:10:25,630 --> 00:10:29,550
Working near the king...
There's no greater honor than that!

146
00:10:29,760 --> 00:10:31,090
Hold on, Marco!

147
00:10:32,510 --> 00:10:35,350
Quit talkin' like a goody-two-shoes
and say what you really think!

148
00:10:35,550 --> 00:10:37,100
You wanna join the Military Police

149
00:10:37,310 --> 00:10:40,640
'cause it means a safe, comfy life in the interior!

150
00:10:40,850 --> 00:10:42,850
No! I really do want to...

151
00:10:43,060 --> 00:10:45,020
It's comfy in the interior?

152
00:10:46,270 --> 00:10:50,030
Until five years ago, this used to be the interior too.

153
00:10:50,240 --> 00:10:53,200
What's your point, Eren?

154
00:10:54,360 --> 00:10:57,490
Jean. You don't need to go to the interior.

155
00:10:57,700 --> 00:11:00,660
I'd say your head is nice
and spacious enough as it is.

156
00:11:03,460 --> 00:11:04,420
You little...

157
00:11:04,620 --> 00:11:08,550
Honing your Titan-killing skills
to get away from the Titans...

158
00:11:08,750 --> 00:11:11,590
Doesn't that seem like a weird system to you?

159
00:11:11,800 --> 00:11:13,430
You only say that now?

160
00:11:13,630 --> 00:11:17,260
I want that stupid system
to stay in place, for my sake.

161
00:11:17,470 --> 00:11:18,560
You piece of scum!

162
00:11:18,760 --> 00:11:20,430
Shut up! This is the real world!

163
00:11:20,640 --> 00:11:21,980
Eren! Quit it!

164
00:11:22,180 --> 00:11:23,890
Stop that.

165
00:11:28,440 --> 00:11:29,860
- Screw you!
- Huh?!

166
00:11:30,070 --> 00:11:31,530
Let go! You're gonna rip it!

167
00:11:31,740 --> 00:11:33,610
I don't give a damn about your clothes! I'm jealous!

168
00:11:33,820 --> 00:11:36,030
Huh?! What are you talking about?!

169
00:11:43,500 --> 00:11:44,620
I see now...

170
00:11:44,830 --> 00:11:49,460
He always has to take his feelings out on others...

171
00:11:49,670 --> 00:11:52,090
Just like I always do.

172
00:11:52,300 --> 00:11:54,260
But not this time!

173
00:11:56,340 --> 00:11:59,470
I'm going to use that move
to take control of the situation!

174
00:12:09,980 --> 00:12:11,780
What the hell was that?!

175
00:12:11,980 --> 00:12:14,110
A combat technique I learned the hard way

176
00:12:14,320 --> 00:12:16,990
while you were screwing around.

177
00:12:18,620 --> 00:12:22,490
A carefree, capricious life
is your idea of the real world?

178
00:12:22,700 --> 00:12:26,620
And you honestly call yourself a soldier?!

179
00:12:35,130 --> 00:12:38,390
I heard a loud sound just now...

180
00:12:38,590 --> 00:12:41,640
Would anyone care to explain?

181
00:12:46,100 --> 00:12:49,480
- It was Sasha. She passed gas.
- Huh?!

182
00:12:49,690 --> 00:12:51,860
You again?

183
00:12:53,190 --> 00:12:55,860
Learn some decency, will you?!

184
00:13:04,830 --> 00:13:10,330
218 cadets went on to reach graduation.

185
00:13:12,670 --> 00:13:14,210
Give your hearts!

186
00:13:14,420 --> 00:13:16,010
Yes, Sir!

187
00:13:16,210 --> 00:13:22,050
You have three options
after you graduate from the Cadets today!

188
00:13:22,260 --> 00:13:26,220
The Garrison Regiment,
which reinforces the walls and protects each city!

189
00:13:26,430 --> 00:13:28,270
The Scout Regiment, which risks life and limb

190
00:13:28,480 --> 00:13:30,690
to venture into Titan territory outside the walls!

191
00:13:30,900 --> 00:13:33,730
And the Military Police Regiment,
which serves under the king

192
00:13:33,940 --> 00:13:35,940
by policing the people and preserving order!

193
00:13:36,150 --> 00:13:39,070
Of course, the only ones
allowed to join the Military Police

194
00:13:39,280 --> 00:13:42,410
are the top ten cadets who were previously named!

195
00:13:48,830 --> 00:13:52,000
We've finally made it here...

196
00:13:52,210 --> 00:13:54,340
Now it's our turn

197
00:13:54,540 --> 00:13:56,840
to devour the Titans!

198
00:14:13,440 --> 00:14:14,150
Yes!

199
00:14:14,360 --> 00:14:15,820
Now I'm gonna be in the Military Police!

200
00:14:16,020 --> 00:14:18,860
No more worrying about food!

201
00:14:19,070 --> 00:14:21,950
How'd I get ranked under Eren?!

202
00:14:22,160 --> 00:14:23,870
Damn!

203
00:14:24,070 --> 00:14:26,870
Are you seriously not gonna join
the Military Police Regiment, Eren?!

204
00:14:27,080 --> 00:14:29,790
Even after you got into the top ten and all?!

205
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:32,500
My mind was set from the very start.

206
00:14:32,710 --> 00:14:36,420
I didn't train all this time to live in the interior.

207
00:14:36,630 --> 00:14:38,590
I did it to fight the Titans.

208
00:14:38,800 --> 00:14:40,470
We can't beat them!

209
00:14:44,390 --> 00:14:48,520
You know how many tens of thousands
of people have been eaten so far...

210
00:14:48,720 --> 00:14:53,100
The answer was clear
after we lost 20% of our population.

211
00:14:53,310 --> 00:14:57,520
Humanity can't beat the Titans.

212
00:15:02,990 --> 00:15:04,490
So?

213
00:15:05,950 --> 00:15:09,200
You're gonna give up
because you think we can't win?!

214
00:15:09,410 --> 00:15:13,460
- Well...
- Yes, humanity has lost so far.

215
00:15:13,670 --> 00:15:16,920
That's because we were clueless about the Titans!

216
00:15:17,130 --> 00:15:20,010
Material warfare is useless against them.

217
00:15:20,210 --> 00:15:25,470
We lost, but the information we gained
in battle will lead to further hope!

218
00:15:25,680 --> 00:15:28,470
Are we just going to throw away
all the advances in fighting techniques

219
00:15:28,680 --> 00:15:32,480
that cost us tens of thousands of lives
so we can be Titan fodder?!

220
00:15:32,680 --> 00:15:34,480
The hell with that!

221
00:15:34,690 --> 00:15:38,190
I'm going to drive out every last Titan

222
00:15:38,400 --> 00:15:40,570
and leave these cramped walls!

223
00:15:40,780 --> 00:15:42,780
That's my dream!

224
00:15:42,990 --> 00:15:46,870
Humanity hasn't truly been defeated yet!

225
00:15:54,370 --> 00:15:56,580
Wait, Eren!

226
00:15:56,790 --> 00:16:00,250
If you wanna go outside the walls, be my guest!

227
00:16:00,460 --> 00:16:03,470
I'm gonna join the Military Police!

228
00:16:13,270 --> 00:16:16,310
Eren. That stuff about your dream just now...

229
00:16:16,520 --> 00:16:18,980
Yeah, I borrowed those ideas of yours

230
00:16:19,190 --> 00:16:21,820
about going outside instead of staying inside.

231
00:16:23,900 --> 00:16:26,200
I'm going to join the Scout Regiment!

232
00:16:27,070 --> 00:16:28,530
Are you serious, Armin?!

233
00:16:28,740 --> 00:16:31,870
You were the top in classroom studies!
You should put that to use!

234
00:16:32,080 --> 00:16:35,620
I won't be a burden. Even if it costs me my life.

235
00:16:35,830 --> 00:16:38,040
I'll join the Scouts too.

236
00:16:38,250 --> 00:16:42,000
Hey! You graduated top of the class!
You should join the Military Police!

237
00:16:42,210 --> 00:16:47,090
If you join the Military Police, then I will too.

238
00:16:47,300 --> 00:16:51,890
If you join the Garrison Regiment, then I will too.

239
00:16:52,100 --> 00:16:56,560
Because you'll die an early death unless I'm around.

240
00:16:56,770 --> 00:16:59,810
I never asked for your help.

241
00:17:00,020 --> 00:17:03,110
I don't want to lose any more of my family.

242
00:17:25,510 --> 00:17:28,630
It's here! The main unit of the Scout Regiment!

243
00:17:28,840 --> 00:17:32,510
Commander Erwin! Give those Titans a real thrashing!

244
00:17:33,510 --> 00:17:36,600
Look! It's Captain Levi!

245
00:17:36,810 --> 00:17:39,690
They say he's as mighty as an entire brigade!

246
00:17:39,890 --> 00:17:42,150
Ugh. Talk about annoying...

247
00:17:42,360 --> 00:17:44,400
This is nothing like five years ago!

248
00:17:44,610 --> 00:17:47,860
People actually feel hopeful about the Scout members!

249
00:17:48,070 --> 00:17:50,820
Yeah, everyone's cheered up since then.

250
00:17:51,030 --> 00:17:53,070
Nothing's happened in five years.

251
00:17:53,280 --> 00:17:55,450
They've upgraded the mounted cannons too.

252
00:17:55,660 --> 00:17:58,040
I doubt the Colossal Titan will show up anymore.

253
00:17:58,250 --> 00:17:59,370
Yeah!

254
00:17:59,580 --> 00:18:02,000
That's a load of crap, you idiotic couple!

255
00:18:02,210 --> 00:18:04,670
Wh-What? Us, a married couple?

256
00:18:04,880 --> 00:18:06,800
You're getting ahead of yourself, Eren!

257
00:18:07,840 --> 00:18:10,050
Hey, guys!

258
00:18:10,260 --> 00:18:11,800
Mr. Hannes!

259
00:18:12,800 --> 00:18:15,470
Heard you graduated yesterday.

260
00:18:15,680 --> 00:18:17,970
Man, you brats have really matured.

261
00:18:18,180 --> 00:18:19,520
You too, Mr. Hannes!

262
00:18:19,730 --> 00:18:22,230
You used to be a drunk, but now
you're chief of the Corps of Engineers.

263
00:18:22,440 --> 00:18:24,060
Oh, you!

264
00:18:25,860 --> 00:18:30,570
I'm sorry I couldn't save your mom.

265
00:18:31,910 --> 00:18:34,870
It wasn't your fault.

266
00:18:35,070 --> 00:18:37,490
We're not ignorant anymore.

267
00:18:37,700 --> 00:18:40,370
We won't let another tragedy like that happen.

268
00:18:41,460 --> 00:18:43,540
We will defeat the Titans!

269
00:18:47,670 --> 00:18:52,050
I don't know if I should be happy
that you've grown up or not...

270
00:18:52,260 --> 00:18:54,180
Don't go dyin', now.

271
00:18:55,890 --> 00:18:56,970
Huh?!

272
00:18:57,180 --> 00:18:59,060
You're joining the Scouts?!

273
00:18:59,270 --> 00:19:01,730
Conny! You were so set on the Military Police!

274
00:19:01,940 --> 00:19:04,850
Yeah, I was! But...

275
00:19:05,060 --> 00:19:07,690
Sounds like your speech yesterday won him over!

276
00:19:07,900 --> 00:19:08,900
Huh?!

277
00:19:09,110 --> 00:19:10,320
M-Mind your own business!

278
00:19:10,530 --> 00:19:13,240
I decided it on my own!

279
00:19:13,450 --> 00:19:15,820
Don't be so embarrassed.

280
00:19:16,030 --> 00:19:17,660
You're not the only one.

281
00:19:19,490 --> 00:19:20,500
Thomas...

282
00:19:20,700 --> 00:19:21,790
You don't mean...?

283
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:24,580
Umm, everyone?

284
00:19:24,790 --> 00:19:28,500
I brought some meat from the officers' storehouse!

285
00:19:29,550 --> 00:19:32,010
Sasha! Do you want to end up
in solitary confinement?!

286
00:19:32,220 --> 00:19:33,550
You really are crazy!

287
00:19:33,760 --> 00:19:35,390
So much it's scary...

288
00:19:35,590 --> 00:19:37,970
We can all share it later...

289
00:19:38,180 --> 00:19:40,600
All sliced up, and between some bread...

290
00:19:41,560 --> 00:19:43,600
- Go put it back!
- Yeah!

291
00:19:43,810 --> 00:19:47,270
After we lost all that land,
meat's become really valuable.

292
00:19:47,480 --> 00:19:49,270
It'll be fine!

293
00:19:52,940 --> 00:19:57,490
We can just raise more cattle and sheep
once we retake our land!

294
00:20:02,080 --> 00:20:03,620
I'll have some of the meat too!

295
00:20:03,830 --> 00:20:07,290
M-Me too! Save me some!

296
00:20:07,500 --> 00:20:09,590
I'll have some too, of course!

297
00:20:09,790 --> 00:20:11,550
Guys...

298
00:20:11,750 --> 00:20:13,670
Why are you just standing there, Eren?

299
00:20:13,880 --> 00:20:16,590
We'll get found out if we don't get back to work!

300
00:20:16,800 --> 00:20:18,640
Lunch isn't for a while!

301
00:20:25,230 --> 00:20:28,100
Five years have passed since then...

302
00:20:28,310 --> 00:20:33,400
Humanity is finally regaining its dignity.

303
00:20:33,610 --> 00:20:35,360
We can win!

304
00:20:37,240 --> 00:20:40,410
Humanity's fight back...

305
00:20:40,620 --> 00:20:42,290
...is just beginning!

306
00:21:02,810 --> 00:21:03,600
Oww! Hot!

307
00:21:03,810 --> 00:21:05,930
Wh-What the...?!

308
00:21:12,270 --> 00:21:14,480
Samuel!

309
00:21:14,690 --> 00:21:16,240
Sasha!

310
00:21:24,160 --> 00:21:25,040
Samuel!

311
00:21:25,240 --> 00:21:27,750
Stay still!

312
00:21:27,960 --> 00:21:29,620
That was close!

313
00:21:32,290 --> 00:21:33,540
The wall...

314
00:21:33,750 --> 00:21:35,380
It's broken!

315
00:21:36,460 --> 00:21:38,680
It's happening again!

316
00:21:38,880 --> 00:21:41,260
The Titans are going to get in!

317
00:21:43,930 --> 00:21:46,180
I'm going to drive out...

318
00:21:46,390 --> 00:21:49,690
...every last one!

319
00:21:49,890 --> 00:21:53,560
Every... last one...

320
00:21:55,690 --> 00:21:57,440
Mounted Cannon Maintenance Squad 4!

321
00:21:57,650 --> 00:21:59,530
Prepare for battle!

322
00:22:00,410 --> 00:22:03,200
The target is the Colossal Titan dead ahead!

323
00:22:03,410 --> 00:22:06,740
This is our chance! Don't let it get away!

324
00:22:16,050 --> 00:22:17,710
Hey, there.

325
00:22:18,840 --> 00:22:20,880
It's been five years since we met.

326
00:22:39,440 --> 00:22:44,370
Your dreams are where your heart is

327
00:22:44,570 --> 00:22:50,620
They're more fragile than life itself

328
00:22:50,830 --> 00:22:55,290
Over and over you cast them aside,
only to find more

329
00:22:55,500 --> 00:23:01,970
Now, rest in peace

330
00:23:02,180 --> 00:23:13,310
Pounding impulses defile the things we wish for

331
00:23:13,520 --> 00:23:23,570
and the more we forget
the more we remember again

332
00:23:23,780 --> 00:23:29,540
In this beautiful, cruel world

333
00:23:29,740 --> 00:23:34,710
all I can do is ask why we're still alive

334
00:23:34,920 --> 00:23:40,420
Oh, with our strength... and our weakness...

335
00:23:40,630 --> 00:23:46,090
what are we going to protect if there's no sense

336
00:23:46,300 --> 00:23:49,720
to anything anymore?

337
00:23:56,560 --> 00:23:59,820
Hell opens its mouth once more.

338
00:24:00,020 --> 00:24:04,320
Titans devour the soldiers
before they can even catch their breaths.

339
00:24:04,530 --> 00:24:08,301
Amid this, Eren saves Armin
from the brink of death, but...

340
00:24:08,301 --> 00:24:09,700
First Battle: The Struggle for Trost, Part 1
Amid this, Eren saves Armin
from the brink of death, but...

341
00:24:09,700 --> 00:24:09,969
First Battle: The Struggle for Trost, Part 1
